  "note": "Two splits. TRAIN is every probe the keyword rules were written or tuned against: the original 35, plus Sol's five fresh probes from review round 3, which the rules were repaired to handle. Its accuracy measures fitting, not generalization, and is reported as such. HOLDOUT is 32 probes written before they were scored and never tuned against; its accuracy is the honest generalization estimate for the keyword pass. Caveat recorded in DONE.md: the hold-out is held out from rule authoring, not from the author, so it is an upper bound on generalization to real model prose rather than a measurement of it.",
